<title>NETHERLANDS: Rotterdam cereals, feed shipments down first half.</title>
<headline>Rotterdam cereals, feed shipments down first half.</headline>
<dateline>ROTTERDAM 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The port of Rotterdam said on Tuesday transshipments of cereals and animal feed were 6.4 million tonnes in the first half of the year, down almost six percent from 1996 due to a &quot;structural&quot; decline in world trade.</p>
<p>The port said high grain prices as a result of generally bad harvests had caused global shipments to decline, a trend that was accentuated by European Union measures, which have led to more grain being consumed within Europe, it added.</p>
<p>--Amsterdam Newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
